  {
    "sha": "cb4acfadd3b3cdef0177523d8fac617f8aa76fd0",
    "node_id": "C_kwDOV1WsOtoAKGNiNGFjZmFkZDNiM2NkZWYwMTc3NTIzZDhmYWM2MTdmOGFhNzZmZDA",
    "commit": {
      "author": {
        "name": "Quintin Smits",
        "email": "qd.smits@gmail.com",
        "date": "2026-11-23T23:20:12Z"
      },
      "committer": {
        "name": "Quintin Smits",
        "email": "qd.smits@gmail.com",
        "date": "2026-11-23T23:20:12Z"
      },
      "message": "fix(gcode): review fixes for bounded cycles, frames, sections and codes\n\nThe review of 92627aef0 on PR #3657 found eleven items. This commit\nfixes items 1-9 and 11:\n\n1. G73/G83 pecks must move strictly deeper and stop at 4096 pecks; one\n   cycle block may emit at most 100 000 moves over pecks and L repeats.\n   Near 1e20 a subtraction of Q left the same f64 and the loop spun.\n2. Lengths, points, cycle levels, hole positions and arc centres must be\n   finite and inside +/-1e6 mm after unit conversion and arithmetic;\n   feed and dwell have ranges; caller options are checked before line 1.\n   New errors: OutOfRange (by line) and InvalidOptions.\n3. One frame rule: the cursor is in the active work frame. A G54-G59\n   change after motion moves it by the origin difference and needs both\n   origins. G28/G30 use the active origin and refuse when it is unknown.\n4. Canned cycles run in G17 only; G18/G19 cycles and plane changes while\n   a cycle is active are refused before expansion.\n5. Spindle, coolant, length- and work-offset changes after a move start a\n   new section at that move boundary (same tool).\n6. Cycle state (sticky R/Z, G98 initial level) holds over contiguous\n   cycle blocks, also when a cycle code is written again.\n7. G89 feeds out to the clear level; G85 feeds to R, then rapids.\n8. Decimal codes keep their place value: G90.10 is G90.1, G90.01 is\n   refused by name.\n9. Haas P with a decimal point is seconds, without one milliseconds.\n11. The three test binaries are one directory suite, tests/parse/\n    (10 -> 37 tests).\n\nRefs #2217\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
